function explainFact(L,V){const m={'ICAO24':'A 24-bit aircraft address broadcast by the transponder. DOAA uses it as the durable observed identity of an airframe; registrations and callsigns can change.','CURRENT CALLSIGN':'The identifier the aircraft is broadcasting for this operation. It usually describes the flight or operator activity, not the physical airframe.','FLIGHT ICAO':'The ICAO-format operational flight identifier. This can differ from the passenger-facing IATA flight number.','FLIGHT IATA':'The shorter passenger-facing flight number used by many airlines and booking systems.','ICAO TYPE':'The standardized aircraft type designator, such as A321 or B38M. It identifies the type, not this individual airframe.','POSITION':'Position is relative to the current DOAA home aerodrome. Track is the direction the aircraft is moving over the ground, which is not necessarily the direction its nose is pointing.','ADS-B CATEGORY':'ADS-B emitter category reported by the aircraft. It describes the broad aircraft/vehicle class, not the exact model.','SQUAWK':'Four-digit transponder code currently being broadcast. Some codes have special operational meanings.','WAKE':'Wake-turbulence category used for separation between aircraft.','CLASS':'Broad propulsion / aircraft class derived from the known type.','ENGINES':'Known engine count and engine family for this airframe or type.','SPECIFICITY':'How closely this media matches the aircraft: exact airframe, representative model, or representative type.','LICENCE':'Reuse licence attached to the media source.','ENCOUNTERS':'Distinct periods in which DOAA observed this airframe. A gap closes one encounter and a later sighting begins another.','SAMPLES':'Individual timestamped ADS-B observations retained by DOAA. Samples are evidence; encounters organize that evidence into sightings.'};return m[L]||null}
